WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.200
We're not going to 'fix' climate change.
Climate change is a thing that we're

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.710
going to be living with now in
perpetual time.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:12.000
There's not going to be a fix for
sea-level rise, or a fix for droughts, or

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.599
anything like that. They're going to be
various adaptations, various ways of

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:19.800
dealing with it, better and worse than
others. But we're not going to fix it.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.600
It's our world now. And this
notion that, you know, the land is here

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.970
the sea is there, and we live in this, in
this...because the world that we see is

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:33.870
the world we think is always going to be
there, and has always been there. What

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:38.460
climate change is teaching us is that
the world is in huge flux, and it's

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.149
moving around very quickly. And we're
gonna have to live in a rapidly-changing

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:48.210
world. And so how do we think differently
in order to embrace that is, I think, one

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.950
of the big questions at the center of
all this.

